WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:02.580
MARTIN: Here is a
pet peeve of mine.

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:05.580
Many companies define what
they aren't instead of

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:06.900
what they are.

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:09.000
It's the same when
we say serverless.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.790
The name says what
it isn't, servers,

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:13.830
but it doesn't say what it is.

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:16.170
This can be confusing
to business people.

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:18.120
Could we come up
with a better name?

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:20.880
One way would be to think
about why organizations

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:22.470
choose to go serverless.

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:25.080
Businesses like the
autoscaling and pay per use

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:26.400
they get from serverless.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.170
But when I talk to
them, most of them

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:32.080
tell me they picked serverless
for two other reasons.

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:34.680
One, it's easier
to hire developers.

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:37.940
They don't have to know Linux
or Kubernetes to be productive.

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:41.340
Two, there is less ops work to
maintain a serverless system

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:42.720
once it's been built.

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:44.340
Maybe our new word
for serverless

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:46.590
should reflect this reality.

00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:48.450
I will keep using
the term serverless

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:50.340
in my videos for now,
just so that people

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:52.050
know what I'm talking about.

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:55.830
But what word would you
prefer instead of serverless?

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:59.090
Let's discuss in
the comments below.

